dx = div64_u64(dx, dsm);
Reason:
Changing `dsm` to `u64` preserves the full 64-bit difference, avoiding zero due to truncation. Replacing `do_div` with `div64_u64` correctly divides a 64-bit dividend by a 64-bit divisor, eliminating the divide-by-zero for large slope values.

